.TH UDECK-TERMINAL-DEFAULT 1 "2026-11-06" "uDeck Terminal 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
udeck-terminal-default \- configure or restore Debian and XDG terminal defaults
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B udeck-terminal-default status
.RI [ --user " USER" ]
.br
.B sudo udeck-terminal-default apply --user USER --acceptance REPORT.json
.br
.B sudo udeck-terminal-default restore --user USER --backup BACKUP.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
Apply requires passing acceptance for the installed build. It registers the
x-terminal-emulator alternative at priority 20 with its manual-page slave,
backs up the previous auto/manual selection, system and user XDG preferences,
and supported desktop bindings. It then selects uDeck Terminal. Existing
desktop-specific user preference lists are updated as well.
Registration is deferred until apply so installation cannot switch an automatic
default before acceptance. Packages never silently change the current default.
.PP
Restore recovers the original files and alternatives mode, and removes a newly
registered alternative. Restoration refuses to overwrite configuration changed
after apply. Keep the backup and reconcile such changes manually.
.SH FILES
.I /var/lib/udeck-terminal/defaults/
contains private, root-owned recovery manifests. Configuration symlinks and
unsupported explicit terminal flags require manual migration before apply.
.SH VERIFICATION
Configuration success does not prove launch behavior. Verify the alternative,
xdg-terminal-exec, Gio Terminal=true, keyboard shortcuts and file managers in
both desktop environments. Rehearse restoration before final default selection.
